<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Notes: Some simulation experiment settings, like training and testing objects and the reward functions in MuJoCo and Isaac Gym, also differ. See Sec. </span><a href="#S6.SS1.SSS2" title="VI-A2 Quantitative Results and Analysis ‣ VI-A Efficacy of DexRep in Grasping ‣ VI Effectiveness of DexRep Across Tasks ‣ DexRepNet++: Learning Dexterous Robotic Manipulation with Geometric and Spatial Hand-Object Representations" class="ltx_ref" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">VI-A2</span></a><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for more details. The results of DAPG, ILAD, and IBS in Isaac Gym are sourced from UniDexGrasp </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">]</span></cite><span id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
